config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_XIAOMI_ROBOT_VACUUM
	bool "Domoticz plugin: Xiaomi robot vacuum"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_GEVENT
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_MSGPACK
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_MIIO
	default n
	help
		control of the Xiaomi and roborock robot vacuums: start, stop, return to base, status and battery (it runs a helper server next to Domoticz with gevent and talks to the vacuum through python-miio).

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/xiaomi-mirobot, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		Setup -> Hardware -> Xiaomi MI Robot, enter the address and the token of the vacuum.

		Upstream ships no license file: the README is installed with the plugin. The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
